id: pm-rlm-v2agg
title: Typed snapshot aggregation and one measured cloud comparison
description: "Budgeted count, sum, distinct, group_count and extrema; frozen-snapshot replay; one pinned seeded cloud evaluation."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T05:53:47.468Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T22:43:16.897Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Six aggregate revert proofs; npm and Bun release gates; one honest 24-question comparison
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[41]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T05:54:26.312Z",codex-agent,"Plan fixed before live inference: six deterministic snapshot aggregates with no evaluation or code execution; len(field) means UTF-8 bytes, numeric fields must be finite, extrema return sorted tied ids, missing text is empty. Reuse existing budget, projection, ledger and replay paths. Pin both public source revisions and verify the same 24 selected questions. One invocation only, no answer tuning; include cheap generic precomputed-tool context arm if it fits."
  "2026-10-19T06:00:47.940Z",codex-agent,"Optional third arm omitted before inference to conserve owner quota: it requires 24 additional full cloud requests. The new harness verifies public visibility, exact historical revisions, complete corpus counts/bytes and all 24 seeded questions/truths before its exclusive once-only marker. Successful new runs are replayed. New raw response evidence stays in ignored local artifacts."
  "2026-10-19T06:01:38.699Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof receipt: count, sum, distinct, group_count, argmax and argmin each independently fail the exact scoped observation regression when only that operation is removed. All six passed behavioral revert verification in node test/v2-revert.ts; source bytes restored. Starting the only authorized cloud invocation with the implementation frozen."
  "2026-10-19T06:02:18.734Z",codex-agent,"Preflight refused before any model request and before creation of the once-only marker: removing the historical answer-format suffix had also changed seeded hash ranking. Preserve that suffix only in the hash input while retaining format-neutral emitted questions. This restores historical task identity rather than selecting a new evaluation set. No cloud quota consumed and no answer-dependent protocol tuning."
  "2026-10-19T06:09:33.391Z",codex-agent,"Both linked release checks passed under isolated Git identity settings: each ran 120/120 tests, 100 percent in all four coverage dimensions across 21 required sources, 72/72 documented declarations, zero duplication and 2/2 packed consumer tests. Added a recorded-shape test afterward (focused suite now 5/5) and strengthened packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx fixtures to demand a delivered count observation before a prose-wrapped finish. The strengthened packed tests pass 2/2. Final gates will run after the measurement/report and tracker writes are complete."
  "2026-10-19T06:15:50.358Z",codex-agent,"Current implementation gates pass under isolated HOME and Git identity: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 121/121 tests plus 2/2 packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Coverage remains 100/100/100/100 over 21 required source files; docstrings 72/72; duplication zero; production audit passes. Packed fixtures verify a delivered count observation and tolerate a prose-wrapped string finish. Source, protocol and eval implementation remain frozen during the one live run. Release workflows remain disabled for automatic publishing."
  "2026-10-19T06:41:40.644Z",codex-agent,"Interim single-run checkpoint: 10/24 questions complete; RLM 0/10, stuffing 0/10; delivered aggregates 5, reads 0. These are interim counts, not the final comparison. Measured code remains at verified source commit 4be91f0; no completed question was retried. Fresh-clone strict tracker health passed. Both complete release gates passed 121 tests plus two packed consumers each."
  "2026-10-19T07:28:28.154Z",codex-agent,"Single authorized glm-5.3:cloud run complete on the original fixed revisions and 24 tasks: RLM 1/24, stuffing 1/24; no accuracy advantage. Mean reported-or-estimated tokens 231491.58 versus 23623.29; seconds 204.60 versus 6.70; requests 32.00 versus 1.00. Child reach 0/24; delivered reads 0, aggregates 13; successful replay 1. RLM outer failures budget 23; tool refusals invalid 754; no model/transport failures in either arm. Most-common constant 2/24, zero 1/24. Observation charge 266 byte-estimated tokens; pending 0. Optional third arm was omitted before inference to avoid 24 additional cloud requests. No completed question was retried or answer-tuned. Measured source hash and commit 4be91f0 reproduce exactly; report and per-question artifact contain every counter."
  "2026-10-19T07:32:36.662Z",codex-agent,"Final full-gate receipt: npx pm test pm-rlm-v2agg --run --progress --timeout 900 passed all three linked commands under isolated HOME and Git identity. Focused suite 6/6. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 122/122 tests plus 2/2 packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Coverage 100/100/100/100 across 21 required sources; docstrings 72/72; duplication zero; production audit, pack allowlist, changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. Report regeneration is byte-identical and makes no model calls. No pm CLI/SDK defects were found; linked result tracking is disabled by project policy, so comments retain the durable receipts. All work stays in the package branch and release remains disabled."
  "2026-10-19T10:24:11.532Z",codex-agent,"Additional orchestrator-authorized measurement: preserve the prior v2 artifacts and the exact historical revisions, seed, 24 questions and truths. The default test:live now selects the constrained harness with a new exclusive marker and separate outputs. Same aggregation tools, same limits, same scoring, separate stuffing answer contract. No inference has run in this round yet; no retries or model substitution will follow provider refusal."
  "2026-10-19T10:52:58.356Z",codex-agent,"Single constrained-run interim checkpoint, not a final result: 8/24 tasks complete; RLM 0/8, stuffing 0/8; 295 invalid actions, 5 delivered aggregates, no reads or child reach. Schema-bearing native requests still return malformed or ambiguous action envelopes. Evaluation continues unchanged on source commit 495a156; no completed question is retried and no protocol, limits or answer scoring is being tuned."
  "2026-10-19T11:02:06.628Z",codex-agent,"Halfway checkpoint from the same invocation: original first corpus complete, 12/24 total tasks; RLM 1/12, stuffing 0/12; 447 invalid actions, 8 delivered aggregates, no reads or child reach. The second frozen corpus is now running. These are interim measurements; implementation, schema, prompts, task selection and limits remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T11:09:10.881Z",codex-agent,"Two-thirds interim receipt: 16/24 tasks complete, RLM 2/16 and stuffing 1/16; 586 invalid actions, 10 delivered aggregates, no reads or children. This is still the one authorized invocation on unchanged source 495a156. Full 24-question counts, usage, time and baselines will be recorded after completion."
  "2026-10-19T11:29:15.382Z",codex-agent,"Only newly authorized glm-5.3:cloud invocation complete on the exact original 24 tasks: RLM 2/24, stuffing 1/24; most-common constant also 2/24 and zero 1/24. RLM mean reported-or-estimated tokens 237461.75, seconds 131.256833, requests 37.458333; stuffing 23630.458333, 8.94475 seconds, one request. RLM total requests 899; stuffing 24. Delivered reads 1, aggregates 13, child reach 0/24, successful replay 2. Invalid actions 883; outer budget failures 22; no model/transport failures. Reasons: ambiguous trailing objects 797, ambiguous envelope 66, truncated object 17, no object 1, invalid JSON 1, schema operands 1. Native endpoint did not enforce the schema. Observation charge 9693; pending 0. Recorded source 495a156 and source hash 1b04b87807ff61eb35263a3b1c81dcf50124b227e6fbbb27c94ea143f72d0a47 reproduce exactly. Model-free report is byte-idempotent; no retries or answer tuning. Third arm omitted to conserve 24 additional cloud requests."
  "2026-10-19T11:34:34.597Z",codex-agent,"Final evaluation report and per-question artifact are linked. Model-free formatter passed through pm test and regeneration is byte-identical. Exactly one new live invocation used the original 24 tasks; no retries or answer tuning. RLM 2/24 versus stuffing 1/24 ties the most-common constant baseline; no recursive-quality claim. Final source passes both complete release gates (128 tests plus two packed consumers each). Measured native source is 495a156; the later OpenAI-only schema correction leaves native action/answer contracts unchanged. Public PR evidence and CI checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/8 . Release stays disabled; items remain open for verification."
  "2026-10-19T16:15:35.188Z",codex-agent,"Review round 4 verified all three unresolved PR 8 findings at 21a7ab0; the latest review body contains no additional outside-diff findings. Plan: explicit scalar type/value ordering with an independent aggregate checkpoint version (missing means legacy); portable escaped-path assertions exercised under Windows path semantics; filter empty report history candidates and identify the missing-history root cause. Add independent behavioral revert proofs and run both release gates under isolated Git identity."
  "2026-10-19T16:22:15.971Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 focused regressions pass 4/4 through pinned pm. Independent revert run passes 7/7: scalar comparator, new-run version stamp, legacy replay selection, legacy resumed reads, unknown-version refusal, portable URL assertions, and empty-history filtering each fail their targeted regression when reverted; files restored byte-for-byte. The Windows check executes the actual URL-test callback with Node Windows path/URL primitives. Legacy replay retains item data and root history bytes. Normal-environment strict health has only the previously recorded external extension-host version skew; integrity and history drift pass. Starting both unchanged-threshold release gates with isolated HOME and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-19T16:40:57.302Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 release evidence: pinned pm ran npm run release:check and bun run release:check successfully with isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Each passes 137/137 tests plus 2/2 actual packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Coverage remains 100/100/100/100 over 23 required source files; all 87 declarations documented; duplication zero at the unchanged threshold. Production audit, pack, identity, changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. Existing development dependency advisory remains pm-rlm-wiav; external extension-host skew was already recorded in pm-rlm-v2parse. No new pm CLI/SDK defect found. Result recording is disabled by project policy; these comments retain the durable receipts. Final revert verification and commit integrity checks follow; no threads will be replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-19T16:41:21.196Z",codex-agent,"Final behavior-only revert verification passed again after both release gates: 7/7 targeted assertions fail independently when each fix is reverted; source restored byte-for-byte. Final source and tracker paths are linked on this item. Claims are released for orchestrator verification; this item remains in progress. Commit identity, privacy, changelog and a fresh-clone tracker health check will be verified before push. PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/8 ."
  "2026-10-19T16:42:44.664Z",codex-agent,"Fresh git clone --no-local of the committed source passes build, identity, changelog and pm health --strict-exit --json. Required merge drivers, integrity and history_drift checks pass; the global extension mismatch is absent under isolated HOME. One nonblocking telemetry queue advisory remains, and telemetry configuration was not changed. Existing history records remain an unchanged byte prefix. Final receipt-only metadata will be included with the code and the exact final commit rechecked before push."
  "2026-10-19T17:07:30.157Z",codex-agent,"Round 5: audited test and scripts for Git show, revision lookups and fixed revisions. Only review-r4-revert.ts reads a branch-local commit; other revision usage is synthetic Git fixture setup or evaluation provenance. Replace the old callback lookup with exact current-source substitutions, guard every transform and run all five committed revert scripts sequentially in a verified depth-one clone of HEAD. Preserve all source bytes and unchanged gate thresholds."
  "2026-10-19T17:08:58.663Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses one exact-snippet transform with explicit occurrence counts, including all five parser-version sites and the adapter import. Every proof clears inherited Node test context so nested assertions execute. The shallow regression clones HEAD over file transport with depth 1, verifies matching HEAD and one available commit, checks current proof bytes, runs all five scripts sequentially with locked dependencies, and checks tracked source restoration. An initial code-plus-tracker commit is needed before this exact-HEAD test can execute."
  "2026-10-19T17:10:24.815Z",codex-agent,"Regression evidence before the implementation commit: the original round-four script fails with invalid object name in a real depth-one clone of the previous HEAD. Removing only the new exact-match assertion makes the guard regression fail with exit 1 and ERR_ASSERTION; original bytes restored. Typecheck and lint pass. Duplication is 0 percent at the unchanged threshold after extracting the common assertion runner and source-restoring harness. Proof instructions are in docs/REVERT-PROOFS.md."
  "2026-10-19T17:20:55.847Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 release receipts on source commit 6523deb: pinned pm ran npm run release:check and bun run release:check successfully with isolated HOME and Git settings. Each passed 144/144 suite tests plus 2/2 actual packed npm and Bun consumers. Each gate ran all five proof scripts in a verified depth-one clone of matching HEAD: constrained 8/8, original 51/51, round-three 5/5, round-four 7/7 and v2 10/10, totaling 81/81 independent behavioral reversions with exact tracked-source restoration. Coverage remains 100/100/100/100 over 23 required sources; 87 documented declarations and zero duplication. Identity, production audit, package, changelog and publish-attestation gates pass. No production code or dependency pins changed. Existing development advisory remains pm-rlm-wiav; no new pm CLI/SDK defect found. History remains append-only. Final receipt-only metadata and a fresh-clone health check follow; release the claim and leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T19:27:05.533Z",codex-agent,"Review round 6: fetched all review threads and every comment (no pagination omissions); two unresolved threads remain: PRRT_kwDOVOym886uDtwB (installed README report targets) and PRRT_kwDOVOym886uDtwK (execution refusal integrity). Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Merged current origin/main before fixes. Plan: package the two reports and their per-question JSON, recompute non-spawn execution refusals using the existing observation path and chronological budget, preserve parser-v1 code-only compatibility and spawn handling, and prove each correction behaviorally before both unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-19T19:33:26.475Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: node test/review-r6-revert.ts passed 4/4 independent reversions. Removing only the packed report artifacts fails the actual tarball-link regression; removing only replay validation fails tampered-aggregate assertions; removing only resume validation fails before-inference integrity assertions; removing only chronological model charges fails the valid recursive-budget replay regression. Each mutation produces exit 1 with an assertion failure, then restores exact current source bytes. Existing parser-refusal comparison paths remain unchanged. The package now includes both reports, their per-question JSON and the shared diagnosis linked by those reports."
  "2026-10-19T19:57:05.385Z",codex-agent,"Full-gate infrastructure retry: the depth-one original proof script exceeded its existing 600-second process deadline during a real cold-cache packed npm consumer installation on the busy host. The duplicate gate was stopped. Increase only the clone-runner deadlines to 1800 seconds per script and 3600 seconds overall; retain every proof, assertion and coverage/duplication threshold. Retry on the installed Node 26 runtime with isolated HOME/Git settings and warm package/compile caches. The initial attempt is not a passing gate receipt."
  "2026-10-19T20:06:43.849Z",codex-agent,"Package completeness follow-through for PRRT_kwDOVOym886uDtwB: walking README reveals the same pre-existing omission for docs/EVAL-DESIGN.md, docs/eval-design.json and docs/EVAL-CLOUD.md. Include those public artifacts as well, and start the real-tarball regression at README so every local Markdown/report link is followed recursively. This covers the complete installed documentation graph rather than only the two new links. Restart both full gates on the expanded package correction. Runtime retry uses only the warm npm cache; compile caching is explicitly disabled for precise V8 coverage."
  "2026-10-19T20:27:40.116Z",codex-agent,"Final source 7be3719 release receipts: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0 on Node 26 with isolated HOME/Git settings, warm npm cache and compile caching disabled. Each passes 149/149 suite tests, 85/85 independent behavioral reversions across six scripts in a verified depth-one clone of matching HEAD (8 constrained, 51 original, 5 round-three, 7 round-four, 4 round-six, 10 v2), and 2/2 real packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Coverage is 100/100/100/100 over all 23 required sources; 88 declarations documented; duplication zero at unchanged thresholds. Production audit, identity, package allowlist, changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. Complete README/report link traversal passes against the real tarball. The two package managers produce the same 67-file archive digest. Original history remains an unchanged byte prefix. Earlier interrupted infrastructure attempts are not passing receipts. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was reproduced; the existing development advisory remains pm-rlm-wiav. Final changes only record these receipts and release ownership; leave the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T21:12:20.397Z",codex-agent,"Review round 7: remote head ab318456 is current and contains origin/main (16 ahead, zero behind). All review threads and comment pages fetched; only PRRT_kwDOVOym886uGvgv is unresolved. Latest CodeRabbit review contains no outside-diff findings. Confirmed validateRecorded rejects v1 code-only execution refusals and reconstructs unsettled response usage from stale reservations before settlement. Preserve strict code matching, validate present reasons for all versions, and retain required reasons for v2/v3. Add real-tracker replay/resume regressions and independent behavioral revert proofs. Normal health has only the previously recorded external pm-github host version skew; no pending merge receipts."
  "2026-10-19T21:15:36.569Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOVOym886uGvgv: node test/review-r6-revert.ts passed 6/6, including two new independent source-only reversions inside validateRecorded. Reverting reported-usage reconstruction to step.reserved makes both new legacy replay/resume assertions fail; reverting only the v1 code-only exception likewise fails both. Each process exits 1 with ERR_ASSERTION and all source bytes are restored. Fixtures use v1-compatible get actions, both missing and explicit parser_version=1, exact original reservation formulas, successful preceding reads and a code-only budget refusal. Completed replay is byte-preserving; resume settles usage and an interrupted checkpoint retries only its missing finish. Wrong codes, altered present reasons and missing v2/v3 reasons are still rejected before inference or history writes. An initial linked focused invocation overlapped the deliberate mutation run and is not counted as a passing receipt; rerun only after source restoration."
  "2026-10-19T21:16:12.912Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test pm-rlm-v2agg --run --progress --match \"node --test test/review-r6.test.ts\" passes after source restoration: 6/6 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. The project disables linked result persistence, so this comment is the durable receipt. Typecheck, lint, zero-percent duplication and generated changelog check pass. Committing the correction and append-only tracker evidence before both full release gates so the depth-one HEAD proof runner verifies the new committed proofs."
  "2026-10-19T21:28:13.728Z",codex-agent,"First full npm gate is not a passing receipt: coverage measured 100/100/100/100 across all required sources, and new replay/resume regressions plus all six review proofs passed, but the shallow constrained proof script rejected the new seventh parser-version site because its guarded inventory still expected six. The two reported suite failures are that subtest and its parent (149/151 passed). Update only the exact expected site count from six to seven; retain guarded replacement, every behavioral assertion and all thresholds. Rerun constrained proofs before recommitting and both complete release gates after that commit."
  "2026-10-19T21:28:22.858Z",codex-agent,"Corrected constrained proof inventory now passes 8/8 independent behavioral reversions with exact source restoration (node test/constrained-revert.ts). No production behavior changed after 3284c1a; only the guarded expected parser-site count changed. Commit this test correction with its tracker receipt, then run npm and Bun release gates in separate checkouts of the same committed head to isolate their coverage/build outputs."
  "2026-10-19T21:49:12.943Z",codex-agent,"Final full release receipts on 0af9140: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0 on Node 26 with isolated HOME/Git settings, warm npm cache and compile caching disabled. Separate checkouts of the same head isolate build and coverage outputs. Each passes 151/151 suite tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, all 87/87 independent behavioral reversions (8 constrained, 51 original, 5 round-three, 7 round-four, 6 review, 10 v2) in a verified depth-one clone, and 2/2 real packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Coverage is 100/100/100/100 across all 23 required sources, 88 documented declarations, zero duplication at unchanged thresholds. Identity, production audit, package contents, changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. Both produce the same 67-file package SHA-1 9e278f3d7fd482f2d9d4733d783b5b62cb46d8ff. PRRT_kwDOVOym886uGvgv is fixed; no finding was refused. Earlier unsuccessful attempts are not counted as passing receipts. The first source commit is 3284c1a; 0af9140 changes only the proof inventory and PM evidence. Existing development advisory remains pm-rlm-wiav; no new PM CLI/SDK defect was reproduced. Fresh no-local clone health passed all ten checks with zero warnings. Re-fetched remote main remains fully contained. Release the claim and leave the item in progress; verify receipt-only commit health and exact pushed-head CI next. No review-thread reply, resolution, merge or release."
  "2026-10-19T22:18:53.713Z",codex-agent,"Review round 8: fetched all review threads with complete comments; three unresolved threads PRRT_kwDOVOym886uH5hO, PRRT_kwDOVOym886uH5hT and PRRT_kwDOVOym886uH5hW are valid. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Remote head 32eda9c includes current main; strict health passes with no pending receipts. Plan: correct report wording, recompute all spawn refusal codes and reasons before replay/resume without writes, retain v1 code-only compatibility, add table-driven tampering regressions and independent behavioral revert proofs. No thread replies, resolutions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-19T22:24:05.505Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: shared spawn admission checks run in live order against chronologically created calls. Read-only validation reuses the observation projection and visits each child once before checking the parent prompt budget. Terminal child messages and post-result completion-hook refusal receipts are persisted and validated; hook receipts apply only on the original visit. V1 code-only observations remain supported; unverifiable historical child messages fail closed. Added ten-case table-driven real-ledger tampering matrix, source-drift formatter regression, nested-integrity and digest-reuse checks. Existing focused recovery suite passes 17/17. Thresholds and dependency pins unchanged; development advisory already tracked in pm-rlm-wiav."
  "2026-10-19T22:27:26.038Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof receipt: pinned pm test pm-rlm-v2agg --run --progress --match review-r6-revert --timeout 600 passes node test/review-r6-revert.ts, 13/13 independent proofs (seven new). Removing spawn validation makes the ten-kind matrix fail; independently removing code comparison, reason comparison or child-message persistence also fails its targeted assertion. Reverting either report correction or the formatter source wording fails the source-drift report regression. Every mutation exits 1 with ERR_ASSERTION and restores source byte-for-byte. Focused matrix/report suite passes 11/11 and the separate nested/reuse check passes 1/1; prior recovery regressions pass 17/17. PM linked-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment records the receipt."
  "2026-10-19T22:30:50.539Z",codex-agent,"Final inventory refinement: added explicit reversed-range, text/offset mismatch and incorrect slice-estimate execution-refusal cases. The table now covers thirteen spawn refusal paths, each with code/reason/missing-reason tampering through replay and resume, completed and unfinished checkpoints, plus v1 code-only recovery. The admission implementation already recomputed these paths. Interrupted the preliminary release runs before completion to freeze the expanded test inventory; those partial runs are not gate receipts."
  "2026-10-19T22:39:33.157Z",codex-agent,"CI correction at 2990af4: all 163 regular/other suite checks passed, but two shallow-clone proof scripts failed (166 total, 163 pass and 3 fail including the parent suite). The old corrective-feedback selector matched three error-message receipts after the new persistence fields; narrowed it to the exact step observation assignment, preserving the one-match guard. Legacy parser-version proof now wraps successful replay/resume in assertions so a regenerated execution-integrity refusal becomes the required assertion failure. Removed redundant partition/child code checks from replay traversal: validateRecorded already rejects them first, making the old alternate-error lines unreachable. No threshold or dependency changes. Both Node 22/26 CI failures are excluded from gate receipts; local partial runs stopped for this correction."
  "2026-10-19T22:43:16.882Z",codex-agent,"CI at 86c6d49 passes all 166/166 tests and all 94/94 behavioral proofs in both Node versions. Unchanged 100-percent branch gate correctly rejects one remaining gap (99.91 overall): earlier integrity validation now rejects the former missing-child-failure fixture before the completed-root/unfinished-call guard. Added a distinct orphaned unfinished-call corruption fixture that reaches and asserts that guard. No production code, thresholds or pins changed. This unsuccessful gate remains excluded from final receipts."
